              "body_sha256": "67b7dc15264c5214c56ad77f37a595518899555eb4aec5ebac04384487cb5f56",
              "body_excerpt": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Ownership check still races**\n\nIf another process replaces the socket path after `ownsConfiguredSocketPath()` validates its inode but before `applySocketPermissions()` runs, the pathname-based `chmod` changes permissions on the replacement inode. Because that operation can succeed, reconfiguration may return success even though the listener no longer owns the path. Apply permissions through the bound socket descriptor or another operation that cannot resolve a different inode between validation and mutation.",
